+## Explicit A/B manifest and Kubernetes naming
+
+Manifest filenames are now symmetrical: `rollout-a.yaml` / `rollout-b.yaml`,
+`route-a.yaml` / `route-b.yaml`, `service-a-stable.yaml` /
+`service-b-stable.yaml`, `service-a-canary.yaml` /
+`service-b-canary.yaml`, and `analysis-template-a.yaml` /
+`analysis-template-b.yaml`. Shared infrastructure manifests remain shared.
+
+Rollouts are named `full-single-service-a` and `full-single-service-b`.
+Application A Services are named `full-single-service-a-stable` and
+`full-single-service-a-canary`. Application B remains unchanged.
+Application A's public OpenShift Route is now `full-single-service-a`;
+B remains `full-single-service-b`. The external A hostname therefore changes.
+
+**Migration warning:** Kubernetes resources cannot be renamed in place. When
+these changes reach `main`, automatic Argo CD pruning creates a replacement A
+Rollout, A Services, and A Route, and removes the old names. The new A uses a
+distinct `app: full-single-service-a` selector. Plan a maintenance window; A
+traffic can briefly return 404/503 while the new Route, VirtualService route,
+Services, and Rollout reconcile. Do not run the prepare/start/promote commands
+while resources are being migrated. B resources are not renamed.
+
+Both application Rollouts use a **TCP socket** readiness and liveness probe
+against named port `http` (TCP/8080). These probes do not issue HTTP requests
+through `/`, so they do not generate HTTP request metrics for Kiali. Kiali should
+primarily show externally generated traffic during steady state. However,
+AnalysisTemplate Jobs still perform three candidate `/color` HTTP requests per
+analysis gate, and any other external callers can appear in Kiali. To view
+traffic generator activity alone, run the generators after analyses finish and
+use a Kiali graph interval excluding those analysis runs. The application has
+no automatic service-to-service calling loop.
+
+The Argo CD Application definition in `argocd/` must also be applied separately
+when opting to deploy; it lies outside the `full-single-service/` source path.
+Its `ignoreDifferences` entries now use A's renamed Services.
+
